##
# The HTML of a content element as the page renders it, e.g. to replace it in a preview after a change: rendered at its
# Fusion path, arguments[fusionPath], the data-__neos-fusion-path attribute it has in an edit mode (renderingMode=inPlace
# keeps the attributes in the HTML, so it can replace the element in the page). The node is the element. Only in a
# rendering mode other than frontend, which needs Neos.Neos:Backend.GeneralAccess, see Neos.Api:FusionPath
#
#   {"html": "<div class=\"neos-contentelement\" data-__neos-fusion-path=\"…\">…</div>"}
#
prototype(Neos.Api:View.FusionPathHtml) < prototype(Neos.Api:View) {
    html = Neos.Api:FusionPath {
        path = ${arguments.fusionPath}
    }
}
